[block
  'ORD-0011-app-on-rust'
  [ctx
    'the spec of EMS-001'
    '.guidelines/.orders/EMS-001/EMS-001.pgml'
  [/ctx]
  [onlyif
    'ORD-0009 closed'
    'ORD-0010 closed'
  [/onlyif]
  [tgt
    'the browser app talks to the Rust engine behind one switch, and glyph-ui.js changes only at its transport'
  [/tgt]
  [cnst
    'the protocol is ADR B: the page posts one request line to /engine on its own origin, and serve-dev.js relays it to glyph-engine with --engine rust, or to glyph-protocol.js'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'the transport is a Core of the same shape as GlyphCore: the twelve calls go through /engine, and the tables, esc, xesc and walk stay the JS core'
  [/cnst]
  [nt
    'run is synchronous: the transport asks with a synchronous request, the one reading that leaves glyph-ui.js untouched; question 9 of the return stays open for the Regent'
  [/nt]
  [nt
    'parse cannot send the live tree: the transport rebuilds segments from the full envelope, and buildXml and serializeAST ask toXML and toAST of the source the segments came from'
  [/nt]
  [nt
    'the engine answers with the repository stores; the templates a page merges stay on the JS path, as question 11 of the return reads it'
  [/nt]
  [ins
    'the switch is one query parameter of the page, engine=relay; without it the page runs on the JS core as it does today'
  [/ins]
  [cmp
    'the app on the Rust engine'
    'the app drives the 114 sources through Rust with the same bytes as through JS, and the JS path still works'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
  [sub
    [eq
      [cmp
        [ctx[/ctx]
      [/cmp]
    [/eq]
  [/sub]
  [elab
    [eq[/eq]
    [sub[/sub]
    [rsn[/rsn]
  [/elab]
  [ref
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/ref]
  [ctx[/ctx]
  [core[/core]
  [core[/core]
  [elab[/elab]
[/block]